Subject: [PATCH] win32compat: fix infinite recursion in pRtlNtStatusToDosError

In pRtlNtStatusToDosError(), the return statement invokes
pRtlNtStatusToDosError(status) recursively instead of calling the resolved
function pointer s_pRtlNtStatusToDosError(status).

When called on Windows during preauth virtual token generation
(generate_sshd_virtual_token -> pRtlNtStatusToDosError), NTSTATUS error
conversion (e.g. mapping STATUS_NO_SUCH_USER to ERROR_NO_SUCH_USER 1317)
enters an infinite tail-call recursion loop pinning 100% of a single CPU core.

Upstream-Repository: PowerShell/openssh-portable
Upstream-Target: contrib/win32/win32compat/w32api_proxies.c
Upstream-Release-v10.0.0.0-Commit: b8c08ef9da9450a94a9c5ef717d96a7bd83f3332
Upstream-Release-v9.5.0.0-Commit: 59aba65cf2e2f423c09d12ad825c3b32a11f408f
Raw-Source-SHA256: 71a4d38ff22cc1812347a93a47241089b9e9fa545a2e834be8b2c250176f9f8c
---
 contrib/win32/win32compat/w32api_proxies.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/contrib/win32/win32compat/w32api_proxies.c
+++ b/contrib/win32/win32compat/w32api_proxies.c
@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@ ULONG pRtlNtStatusToDosError(NTSTATUS status)
 		if ((s_pRtlNtStatusToDosError = (RtlNtStatusToDosErrorType)get_proc_address(hm, "RtlNtStatusToDosError")) == NULL)
 			return STATUS_ASSERTION_FAILURE;
 	}	
-	return pRtlNtStatusToDosError(status);
+	return s_pRtlNtStatusToDosError(status);
 }
 
NTSTATUS pLsaClose(LSA_HANDLE lsa_h)
